# pq-devnet-4 bootnodes (QUIC multiaddrs)
#
# There is NO permanent public bootnode list in Ream (or on leanroadmap).
# Ream's Lean default file is empty:
#   https://github.com/ReamLabs/ream/blob/master/crates/networking/p2p/resources/lean_peers.yaml
# Ream joins a mesh the same way we do: operator / lean-quickstart
#   genesis/nodes.yaml  →  ENRs or QUIC multiaddrs for that run.
#
# Without entries below, `ethean start --network pq-devnet-4` is an
# intentional offline smoke (QuicSwarm binds, duty loop runs). That is OK.
#
# To dial a live mesh, paste one multiaddr per line, for example:
# /ip4/203.0.113.10/udp/9000/quic-v1/p2p/12D3KooWExamplePeerIdReplaceMe
#
# Sources for real addrs (when an interop run is up):
#   - lean-quickstart genesis/nodes.yaml (convert ENR → /ip4/…/udp/…/quic-v1/p2p/…)
#   - Telegram / operator paste for that pq-devnet-4 session
#   - Local two-process mesh: use peer A's logged dialable=… (127.0.0.1)
#
# Also accepted via:
#   ethean start --network pq-devnet-4 --bootnodes '<addr1>,<addr2>'
#   ETHEAN_BOOTNODES='<addr1>,<addr2>'
